# {{ PROJECT_NAME }} — Agent workflow

This project uses the agentic workflow. All workflow configuration lives in the Agentbase directory.

Claude is one host, not the product. This file is the shared workflow body. Host adapters copy it into that host's entry. Hooks that belong to the Claude Code runtime stay on that runtime. Other hosts do not run those hooks automatically.

---

## Section 1: Shared behavior and the backlog

> **Shared philosophy for every agent:** `ORCHESTRATION.md` (plan mode, subagent strategy, self-improvement loop, verification, autonomous error recovery).
> **Self-improvement lessons:** `LESSONS.md` — rules derived from user corrections; review them at the start of a session.
> **Backlog CLI usage:** see `BACKLOG.md`.
> The only task source is the `backlog/` directory. Do not hand-edit task files. Use the `backlog` CLI.

The core loop is the same on every host:

1. Task: read the backlog item, implement only that scope, and run the verification named in its acceptance checks.
2. Review: review the diff for correctness, silent failures, and regressions before closing the task.
3. Commit: commit completed non-sensitive work in the same session without asking. Do not push unless the user asks.

